<%#
  The run as one growing list: every step answered so far, then the step being
  answered now.

  This is what replaces the wizard's one-card-at-a-time page. The problem it
  solves is orientation — an agent on a call losing their place because the page
  jumps and resets every step — not re-reading, which is why rows carry a
  summary rather than the script. Expanding a row read-only is a later change,
  and the entries already record what it will need.

  Both runners render this; the difference between them lives in the shells,
  which pass everything route-shaped as a local.

  locals: scenario, step, next_url, stop_url, back_button, show_cancel,
          errors, submitted, auto_advance
%>
<% entries = runner_thread_entries(scenario) %>
<ol class="runner-thread" id="runner-thread">
  <% entries.each do |entry| %>
    <% if entry["kind"] == "group_start" %>
      <%= render "runner/thread_group", entry: entry %>
    <% else %>
      <%= render "runner/thread_row", entry: entry %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>

  <% if step %>
    <%= render "runner/thread_card",
          scenario: scenario, step: step, next_url: next_url, stop_url: stop_url,
          back_button: back_button, show_cancel: show_cancel,
          errors: errors, submitted: submitted, auto_advance: auto_advance %>
  <% end %>
</ol>
